**Read:** [Air-cleaning systems — DOE-HDBK-1169-2022](../sources/Air-Cleaning-Handbook-DOE.lingua#r_09QPEZ76E9W6HS7R55X2K8TB3X), sections 4.1.1–4.1.4; revisit particle mobility, impaction and collection.

Penetration P is downstream amount divided by upstream amount under matched flow and sampling conditions; efficiency is 1−P. Specify particle size, shape, charge, flow, loading and whether amount means number or mass. A nameplate class is tied to its test method and edition.

Fibrous capture combines diffusion, interception, inertia and sometimes electrostatic effects. It is not simply sieving through holes smaller than each particle. The most penetrating size is a system-dependent minimum of capture, not a universal smallest removable particle.

**Work:** For equal numbers of hypothetical spherical particles of diameters 0.1 and 1 µm with equal density, use efficiencies 0.50 and 0.99. Compute overall number efficiency and mass efficiency separately. Explain why reporting only the more favorable number could misrepresent protection of a size-sensitive process.

